From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] scsi: ufs: disable timestamp for Kioxia THGJFJT2T85BAT0C

The Kioxia UFS device used by the AYN Odin 3 identifies as
THGJFJT2T85BAT0C but rejects the UFS qTimestamp attribute write. This
causes repeated messages such as:

    ufshcd_dev_cmd_completion: unexpected response in Query RSP: fd
    ufshcd_query_attr_qword: opcode 0x04 for idn 48 failed, ... err = -22

The device is otherwise usable. Treat it like the other Kioxia devices
that do not implement qTimestamp and skip the optional timestamp write.

---
 drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c b/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
--- a/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
@@ -318,6 +318,9 @@ static const struct ufs_dev_quirk ufs_fixups[] = {
 	{ .wmanufacturerid = UFS_VENDOR_TOSHIBA,
 	  .model = "THGJFJT0E25BAIP",
 	  .quirk = UFS_DEVICE_QUIRK_NO_TIMESTAMP_SUPPORT },
+	{ .wmanufacturerid = UFS_VENDOR_TOSHIBA,
+	  .model = "THGJFJT2T85BAT0C",
+	  .quirk = UFS_DEVICE_QUIRK_NO_TIMESTAMP_SUPPORT },
 	{ .wmanufacturerid = UFS_VENDOR_TOSHIBA,
 	  .model = "THGJFJT1E45BATP",
 	  .quirk = UFS_DEVICE_QUIRK_NO_TIMESTAMP_SUPPORT },
